# R/03_reviewer_response_analyses

Additional analyses carried out in response to reviewer comments during
peer review.

Each script in this folder addresses one specific point raised by the
reviewers and produces the corresponding table(s) in the Supplementary
Information. Two exploration scripts collect and summarise the raw output
of the two most computation-heavy analyses.

## Files

| Script | Reviewer comment | Produces |
|---|---|---|
| `etas_nonstationary_background_robustness_check.R` | Reviewer 1, points 1–2: scope of the model relative to genuinely nonstationary ETAS formulations; robustness to an unmodelled linear trend in the background rate | SI Sec. S2.5, Tables S9–S11 |
| `etas_coverage_bootstrap.R` | Reviewer 1, point 3: coverage of conditional vs. parametric-bootstrap confidence intervals for the background regression coefficients, validated on simulated data with known truth | SI Sec. S2.6, Table S12 |
| `catalog_completeness_analysis.R` | Reviewer 1, point 5 / Reviewer 3: completeness magnitude $M_c$ vs. the estimation threshold $M_0$ | SI Sec. S3.1, Table S13 |
| `m0_sensitivity_application.R` | Reviewer 1, point 5 / Reviewer 3: sensitivity of the empirical application to the completeness threshold $M_0$ | SI Sec. S3.1, Tables S14–S15 |
| `etas_application_bootstrap.R` | Reviewer 1, point 3: parametric bootstrap of the complete alternating procedure, applied directly to the empirical fit reported in the main text | SI Sec. S3.2, Table S16 |
| `explore_nonstationary_results.R` | — (exploration/reporting) | Console tables and diagnostic plots for `etas_nonstationary_background_robustness_check.R` |
| `explore_coverage_bootstrap_results.R` | — (exploration/reporting) | Console tables and diagnostic plots for `etas_coverage_bootstrap.R` |

## Notes

- These scripts depend on the estimator definitions in
  `R/01_core_estimation/` and, for the application-related analyses, on
  the fitted model from `R/02_application/`.
- Several scripts are computationally intensive (parametric bootstraps
  with 30–150 replicates, each requiring a full refit of the alternating
  ETAS-P procedure) and checkpoint their progress incrementally, so they
  can be safely interrupted and resumed. See the comment header of each
  script for the relevant environment variables (mode of execution,
  number of parallel cores, output directory).
